WEBVTT

1
00:00:11.536 --> 00:00:17.799
Marilla's newly adopted twins, Davy and Dora, were not noticeably alike, although both were fair.

2
00:00:19.119 --> 00:00:22.040
Dora had long curls that always looked perfect.

3
00:00:22.801 --> 00:00:26.742
Davy had a crop of fuzzy little yellow ringlets all over his round head.

4
00:00:27.783 --> 00:00:30.144
Dora's hazel eyes were gentle and mild.

5
00:00:30.784 --> 00:00:32.385
Davy's eyes were mischievous.

6
00:00:33.985 --> 00:00:38.926
After the twins had arrived at Green Gables and unpacked, they had their first dinner with their new

7
00:00:38.966 --> 00:00:46.369
family. At the dinner table, Dora behaved like a little lady, but Davy's manners left much to be

8
00:00:46.409 --> 00:00:52.591
desired. "I'm so hungry I don't have time to eat politely," he said when Marilla scolded him.

9
00:00:52.611 --> 00:00:57.272
"That cake's really delicious," Davy said.

10
00:00:58.548 --> 00:01:02.791
"We haven't eaten cake for so long because mother was too sick to make it.

11
00:01:03.311 --> 00:01:04.492
Can I have another piece?"

12
00:01:05.853 --> 00:01:09.896
Marilla would have refused, but Anne cut a generous second slice.

13
00:01:11.217 --> 00:01:14.899
As she passed it to Davy, she reminded him that he should say thank you.

14
00:01:15.760 --> 00:01:18.642
Davy merely grinned at Anne and took a huge bite.

15
00:01:19.703 --> 00:01:25.087
When Davy had finished the slice he said, "If you'll give me another piece, I'll say thank you."

16
00:01:26.468 --> 00:01:31.167
"No, you've had plenty of cake," said Marilla in a stern tone.

17
00:01:32.328 --> 00:01:37.531
Davy winked at Anne and then snatched Dora's first piece of cake, from which she had taken only

18
00:01:37.711 --> 00:01:38.912
one dainty little bite.

19
00:01:40.033 --> 00:01:43.355
He opened his mouth wide and crammed the whole slice in.

20
00:01:44.316 --> 00:01:47.819
Dora's lip trembled, and Marilla was speechless with anger.

21
00:01:48.559 --> 00:01:55.104
Anne promptly exclaimed, in her best schoolteacher's voice, "Davy, gentlemen don't do things like that."

22
00:01:56.876 --> 00:02:00.177
"I know they don't," said Davy, as soon as he could speak.

23
00:02:00.197 --> 00:02:02.598
"But I'm not a gentleman."

24
00:02:02.618 --> 00:02:05.058
"Don't you want to be?"

25
00:02:05.538 --> 00:02:06.219
said Anne.

26
00:02:06.239 --> 00:02:10.040
"Of course I do," said Davy.

27
00:02:10.060 --> 00:02:13.361
"But you can't be a gentleman till you grow up."

28
00:02:14.541 --> 00:02:18.122
"You can start to be a gentleman now, Davy," Anne said.

29
00:02:18.142 --> 00:02:22.623
"And gentlemen never snatch things or forget to say thank you."

30
00:02:22.643 --> 00:02:26.944
"Gentlemen don't have much fun," said Davy.

31
00:02:26.964 --> 00:02:29.126
"I think I'll wait till I'm grown up."

32
00:02:30.767 --> 00:02:37.690
"Davy and Dora, it's time for bed," said Marilla, who was exhausted and wondering how she would ever

33
00:02:37.790 --> 00:02:38.791
cope with Davy.

34
00:02:39.751 --> 00:02:43.133
Marilla would remember the first week with the twins forever.

35
00:02:44.414 --> 00:02:48.956
It wasn't so different from the second week or the third week, but by the third week she

36
00:02:48.997 --> 00:02:50.297
was used to life with them.

37
00:02:51.078 --> 00:02:54.980
It seemed that Davy was always causing mischief or devising it.

38
00:02:56.832 --> 00:03:01.534
Davy's first major exploit occurred two days after his arrival, on Sunday morning.

39
00:03:02.334 --> 00:03:05.095
Anne dressed him for church while Marilla looked after Dora.

40
00:03:05.995 --> 00:03:08.856
Davy objected strongly to having his face washed.

41
00:03:09.996 --> 00:03:13.417
"Marilla washed it yesterday, and that's enough for one week.

42
00:03:13.938 --> 00:03:15.638
It's more comfortable being dirty."

43
00:03:15.658 --> 00:03:21.300
"Paul Irving washes his face every day by himself," said Anne.

44
00:03:23.084 --> 00:03:28.828
Davy had been living at Green Gables for little over 48 hours, but he already worshipped Anne and

45
00:03:28.948 --> 00:03:31.969
hated Paul Irving, even though he hadn't met him yet.

46
00:03:33.290 --> 00:03:37.153
Anne had praised Paul enthusiastically the day after Davy's arrival.

47
00:03:38.173 --> 00:03:41.915
If Paul Irving washed his face every day, that settled it.

48
00:03:42.576 --> 00:03:44.717
He, Davy Keith, would do it too.

49
00:03:46.338 --> 00:03:49.080
At church Davy behaved quite well at first.

50
00:03:50.196 --> 00:03:53.499
He looked at all the boys and wondered which one was Paul Irving.

51
00:03:53.980 --> 00:03:56.883
But then Davy looked at the girl sitting in front of him.

52
00:03:58.164 --> 00:04:00.906
She was dressed in a violet dress with a frilly neck.

53
00:04:01.747 --> 00:04:06.672
Davy thrust his hand into his pocket and produced a furry, squirming caterpillar.

54
00:04:08.113 --> 00:04:11.797
Marilla saw Davy and tried to grab him, but she was too late.

55
00:04:12.337 --> 00:04:14.760
Davy dropped the caterpillar down the girl's neck.

56
00:04:16.304 --> 00:04:20.766
In the middle of the minister's prayer, there was a series of piercing shrieks.

57
00:04:21.627 --> 00:04:23.668
The minister stopped and opened his eyes.

58
00:04:24.868 --> 00:04:26.049
Every head turned.

59
00:04:26.889 --> 00:04:32.132
Laura White was dancing up and down on the church pew, clutching frantically at the back of her

60
00:04:32.192 --> 00:04:44.864
dress. "Oh, Mommy, Mommy!

61
00:04:44.884 --> 00:04:45.205
Eek! Get it out!

62
00:04:45.225 --> 00:04:46.065
That bad boy put it down my neck!

63
00:04:46.085 --> 00:04:46.926
Mommy, it's going further down.

64
00:04:46.946 --> 00:04:47.386
Ahh!" Mrs.

65
00:04:47.487 --> 00:04:49.608
White rose and carried the hysterical Laura out of church.

66
00:04:49.628 --> 00:04:54.873
Marilla and Anne held Davy firmly for the rest of the church service, and their faces stayed a

67
00:04:54.933 --> 00:04:55.593
bright red.

68
00:04:56.734 --> 00:05:01.678
When they got home, Marilla put Davy to bed and made him stay there for the rest of

69
00:05:01.718 --> 00:05:02.119
the day.

70
00:05:03.039 --> 00:05:04.961
Later Anne went into his room.

71
00:05:04.981 --> 00:05:12.927
"I suppose," Davy said, "that Paul Irving wouldn't have dropped a caterpillar down a girl's neck in church,

72
00:05:13.127 --> 00:05:13.488
would he?"

73
00:05:15.324 --> 00:05:18.325
"Indeed he wouldn't," said Anne sadly.

74
00:05:18.345 --> 00:05:23.006
"Well, I'm kind of sorry I did it then," said Davy.

75
00:05:23.026 --> 00:05:25.787
"But it was such a big caterpillar.

76
00:05:26.628 --> 00:05:28.068
It seemed a pity to waste him.

77
00:05:29.048 --> 00:05:31.989
And say, wasn't it fun to hear that girl yell?"

78
00:05:33.030 --> 00:05:34.590
Anne looked sternly at Davy.

79
00:05:35.510 --> 00:05:40.332
"I did something else today," Davy went on in a muffled voice.

80
00:05:42.356 --> 00:05:45.877
"I'm sorry now, but I'm awful scared to tell you."

81
00:05:45.897 --> 00:05:49.759
"Davy, what is it you've done?"

82
00:05:50.259 --> 00:05:50.920
Anne asked.

83
00:05:50.940 --> 00:05:54.421
"I put a toad in Marilla's bed.

84
00:05:55.601 --> 00:05:57.302
You can go and take it out if you like.

85
00:05:57.882 --> 00:06:01.364
But say, Anne, wouldn't it be fun to leave it there?"

86
00:06:02.964 --> 00:06:03.905
"Davy Keith!"

87
00:06:05.305 --> 00:06:09.547
Anne sprang from Davy's clinging arms and ran across the hall to Marilla's room.

88
00:06:10.407 --> 00:06:11.828
The bed was slightly rumpled.

89
00:06:12.952 --> 00:06:18.236
Anne nervously drew back the blankets and there was the toad, blinking at her from under a pillow.

90
00:06:18.256 --> 00:06:21.499
"How can I carry that awful thing out?"

91
00:06:21.959 --> 00:06:25.562
moaned Anne with a shudder, and then she got a shovel from the yard.

92
00:06:25.582 --> 00:06:31.707
"With Davy at home and Anthony Pye at school, my nerves are almost worn out!"

93
00:06:32.087 --> 00:06:32.788
thought Anne.
